    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="1149" n="991" xml:id="pg991"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Japanese
                    Chargé</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 266.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note No. 21, of the 3d
                    instant, stating that your Government desires to establish a reciprocal
                    exemption of steamboat inspection as between the vessels of the United States
                    and Japan, under the provisions of section 4400 of the Revised Statutes of the
                    United States, and that the Japanese Government is prepared to issue orders
                    exempting American vessels from inspection upon the assurance that the United
                    States Government will issue similar orders exempting Japanese vessels, I have
                    the honor to inform you that the department has received a letter, dated the
                    12th instant, from the Secretary of Commerce and Labor, in which he says: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I have the honor to give the assurance, under the terms of section 4400
                            of the Revised Statutes of the United States, that as soon as an order
                            shall have been issued by the proper authorities of the Empire of Japan
                            exempting steamers of this country in all ports of the Empire of Japan
                            from inspection other than is necessary to establish the fact that the
                            condition of the vessel and her boilers and life-saving equipment are as
                            stated in her current certificate, this department, upon being informed
                            in the usual manner of said action by the Japanese authorities, will at
                            once issue an order granting similar exemption in the ports of the
                            United States to steamers of the Empire of Japan.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
